**Key Features — GIO Glamour Silk Matt (Best Seller)**

- Rich Matt finish — luxurious look

- Fully washable — easy to clean

- Anti-fungal formulation

- Low VOC — safe for family and children

- Available in all shade card colours

**Coverage and Application**

**Q: How much area does 1 bucket (20 Lt) cover?**

A: One 20 Lt bucket covers approximately 1,000 sq ft in 2 coats.

**Q: How many coats are recommended?**

A: 2 to 3 coats are recommended for the best finish and colour depth.

**Q: What pack sizes are available?**

A: We have all sizes: 1 Lt, 4 Lt, 10 Lt, and 20 Lt buckets.

**Q: Do you provide colour consultation?**

A: Yes! We offer colour shade cards and free colour consultancy. Our team will help you choose the perfect shade for your space.

**Common Customer Questions — Interior**

**Q: I need paint for my home but I don****'****t know what quality was used last time.**

A: No problem! Share a photo of your wall or describe its current condition. Our team will visit your site for a FREE inspection and recommend the best product matching or upgrading your previous paint. We can identify the quality from the surface finish.

**Q: I need paint for my home but I don****'****t have a good painter.**

A: We have 5 specialised contractors with 10+ painters each. All are trained and experienced. We provide complete painting service from surface preparation to final coat. Book a FREE site visit and we will arrange everything.

**Q: I need my house painted as soon as possible — urgent requirement.**

A: We understand urgency! Call or WhatsApp us immediately. For urgent jobs in Karnal we can arrange painters within 24-48 hours. A typical 2BHK takes 10 days for a complete professional finish.

**Q: I need paint for damp areas — walls are wet and peeling.**

A: Damp walls need special treatment. We recommend: (1) Dr. Fixit or Asian Waterproofing primer as a base coat, (2) Anti-fungal interior emulsion as topcoat. We also provide a waterproofing service with company guarantees of 1, 5, or 10 years. Book a FREE site visit for proper diagnosis.

**Q: The colour on my wall does not match the shade card.**

A: Colour variation can happen due to lighting, surface texture, or number of coats. We recommend: (1) Apply 2-3 coats for true colour, (2) View shade cards in natural daylight, (3) Get a small trial pot first. Contact us and we will help resolve this immediately.

